# PiSky on Apache.
#
# The installer configures lighttpd, but a station can end up served by Apache
# instead — Allsky installs it, and a reverse proxy in front of the Pi is often
# Apache too. Without this the clean API routes answer 404, which is enough on
# its own to keep a station off the shared map.
#
# This grants the PiSky web root the override the shipped .htaccess needs.
# Nothing here serves the site; it only permits the rules that already ship
# beside the handler.
<Directory "XX_PISKY_WEBROOT_XX">
	# FileInfo is what mod_rewrite directives in .htaccess require.
	AllowOverride FileInfo Options Indexes
	Require all granted
</Directory>
